// ============================================================================
// PLAYER INTENT LIFECYCLE (v9.10)
// ============================================================================
// Player actions took several different shapes. `sendPlayerAction` fired a
// fire-and-forget message; `submit_request` used the pendingRequests queue;
// weapon and spell transactions had their own `dedupeKey`; movement was
// optimistic with a silent server correction. Four mechanisms, four failure
// modes, and one consequence in common: **the UI told the player it had worked
// before the host had agreed.** A rejected move snapped back with no
// explanation; a duplicate tap could double-spend on a slow link.
//
// One lifecycle now covers movement, attacks, spells, rests, HP changes,
// action-economy corrections and character edits:
//
//   PlayerIntent  --(sent)-->  host validates  -->  IntentResult
//        |                                              |
//   optimistic preview                          accepted / corrected / rejected
//        |                                              |
